Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage for the requested‑ad search  
• “ad_format_type”         : limit to IMAGE ads  
• “topic”                  : find Health‑related ads (e.g. ILIKE ‘%Health%’)  
• “advertiser_verification_status” : keep only VERIFIED advertisers  
• “advertiser_location”    : keep advertisers located in Cyprus (“CY”)  
• “region_stats”           : Variant column that (after FLATTEN) supplies  
    –  “region_code”  -> must contain “HR” (Croatia)  
    –  “first_shown”  -> must be  > ‘2023‑01‑01’  
    –  “last_shown”   -> must be  < ‘2024‑01‑01’  
    –  “times_shown_availability_date” -> must be NULL  
    –  “times_shown_upper_bound”       -> used to pick the highest value  
• “audience_selection_approach_info” : Variant column that has to show each of  
    “demographic_info”, “geo_location”, “contextual_signals”, “customer_lists”,  
    “topics_of_interest” NOT equal ‘UNUSED’ (ex. ‘CRITERIA_INCLUDED …’)  
• “creative_page_url”      : the URL we finally need  

Conditions we will need  
1. "ad_format_type" = 'IMAGE'  
2. "topic" ILIKE '%Health%'  
3. "advertiser_verification_status" = 'VERIFIED'  
4. "advertiser_location" = 'CY'  
5. FLATTEN("region_stats") with "region_code" = 'HR'  
6. "region_stats".value:"times_shown_availability_date" IS NULL  
7. "region_stats".value:"first_shown"  > '2023‑01‑01'  
8. "region_stats".value:"last_shown"   < '2024‑01‑01'  
9. In "audience_selection_approach_info" every key mentioned above <> 'UNUSED'  
10. Order by "times_shown_upper_bound" DESC limit 1 to get the largest value  

Below are ten exploratory ➜ final Snowflake SQL queries (each with LIMIT 20) to drill down from simple checks to the final answer.  
(Be sure your session is using database GOOGLE_ADS and schema GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER before running.)

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: Quick look at distinct ad formats available.
SELECT DISTINCT "ad_format_type"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: Inspect sample ‘topic’ values that mention Health.
SELECT DISTINCT "topic"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS"
WHERE "topic" ILIKE '%health%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: Sample verified advertisers located in Cyprus.
SELECT DISTINCT "advertiser_id", "advertiser_disclosed_name", "advertiser_location"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS"
WHERE "advertiser_verification_status" = 'VERIFIED'
  AND "advertiser_location" = 'CY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: Flatten region_stats to view distinct region codes served.
SELECT DISTINCT rs.value:"region_code"::STRING AS "region"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."region_stats") rs
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣ Description: Ads that served in Croatia (HR) and have available times_shown data (times_shown_availability_date IS NULL).
SELECT t."creative_id", rs.value:"region_code"::STRING AS "region", rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date" AS "avail_date"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."region_stats") rs
WHERE rs.value:"region_code"::STRING = 'HR'
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣ Description: Croatian‑served ads whose first_shown > 2023‑01‑01 and last_shown < 2024‑01‑01.
SELECT t."creative_id",
       rs.value:"first_shown"::STRING   AS "first_shown",
       rs.value:"last_shown"::STRING    AS "last_shown"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."region_stats") rs
WHERE rs.value:"region_code"::STRING = 'HR'
  AND rs.value:"first_shown"::STRING >  '2023-01-01'
  AND rs.value:"last_shown"::STRING  < '2024-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣ Description: Examine audience_selection_approach_info keys/values for one Cyprus advertiser ad.
SELECT t."creative_id",
       asi.value
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => OBJECT_KEYS(PARSE_JSON(t."audience_selection_approach_info"))) asi
WHERE t."advertiser_location" = 'CY'
  AND t."creative_id" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣ Description: Ads with all required audience selection approaches NOT ‘UNUSED’.
SELECT "creative_id", "audience_selection_approach_info"
FROM GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER."CREATIVE_STATS"
WHERE TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"demographic_info"      IS NOT NULL
  AND TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"demographic_info"     != 'UNUSED'
  AND TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"geo_location"         IS NOT NULL
  AND TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"geo_location"        != 'UNUSED'
  AND TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"contextual_signals"   IS NOT NULL
  AND TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"contextual_signals"  != 'UNUSED'
  AND TRY_TO_VARIANT("audience_selection_approach_info"):"customer_lists"       IS NOT NULL
